@@ -164,6 +164,8 @@ Each user can have multiple characters in multiple campaigns simultaneously. The
 
 When a player submits a join request, the character appears on the GM's roster in the `pending` list. The GM can **approve** (status → `active`, character is broadcast to all active players) or **reject** (status → `unaffiliated`, character is detached from the campaign and returned to the player's unaffiliated pool).
 
+On the Lightkeeper's desk the requests are on the Requests page (a tab, or Join requests in the phone's drawer), whose count says how many wait, with Invite player under them. A request the Lightkeeper has not been shown pops up at the foot of the screen with Approve, View sheet and Reject, and Later to put it away; it pops up once per browser, so one that came while the desk was closed pops up when it opens.
+
 ### Can an approved investigator leave, or be taken off the roster?
 
 Yes, at any time, before or after the seal (`POST /campaign/release/{id}`). The Lightkeeper releases a member from the foot of that member's sheet, and a player leaves from the foot of their sheet on the desk or from the investigator's row in the hub's registry; both are two-press confirms that say what will happen. The investigator goes back to its player as `unaffiliated` (it is kept, so old log lines, notebook entries and the Circle History still read) and can join this or another campaign by the normal join flow. Its assignment ends as at Retire: its spend count, ability uses, gear and any Train dice it held are cleared. Its circle votes, its relationships (agreed and proposed, at both ends) and its report for the current assignment are dropped, so the "N of M filed" count and the key tally count only the members left. Each resource's maximum is 1 plus the members again: after the seal any of Stitch, Refresh and Train above it is lowered to it, nothing is refunded and nothing goes up; before the seal all three fill to it, as an approval fills them. Every desk is told live, and the Activity Log says "The Lightkeeper released <name> from the circle." or "<name> left the circle." (no reason shown). A dead investigator cannot be released: it stays with the campaign.
